meta {
  name: Link Flight Request to Mission
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/planning/flight-requests/link
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "request_id": {{request_id}},
    "mission_id": 123
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  Links an ACKNOWLEDGED flight request to a PLANNED or IN_PROGRESS mission (pilot_mission).
  The request becomes ASSIGNED and the client's DCC receives /acceptance with the drone of the mission's system.

  From then on the request status follows the mission on the Daily Board — there is no manual status endpoint:
  PLANNED → ASSIGNED, IN_PROGRESS → IN_PROGRESS (/execution), COMPLETED → COMPLETED (/termination result 1),
  ABORTED/CANCELLED → ISSUE (/termination result 0).

  If the mission is waiting for OPM approval and the request's location is inside the mission system's
  operation zones, the mission is approved automatically (autoApproved: true).

  Errors: 404 request/mission not found, 409 request not ACKNOWLEDGED / already linked / mission closed.
}
